        "content": "<p>I have</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Assignment</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">},</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Assignment.restrict</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊆</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Assignment</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Assignment</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">⟩</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>and need to rewrite a sum over <code>Assignment (X ∪ Y ∪ Z)</code> into one over <code>Assignment ((X ∪ Z) ∪ Y)</code>, since the sets are equal.</p>\n<p><code>rw</code> with the set equality fails: \"motive is not type correct\", because the subset proof inside <code>restrict</code> mentions the set. <code>rw [Finset.union_assoc, ...]</code> fails the same way. Going via <code>Equiv.tsum_eq</code> with a transport equivalence lands me inside <code>Equiv.Set.union</code> internals that <code>simp</code> won't unfold.</p>\n<p>Is there an idiomatic way to handle set-equality transport for dependent function types indexed by <code>Finset</code> subtypes? Or is the right move to avoid the situation entirely by choosing one canonical union order everywhere?</p>",
        "id": 617757325,
        "sender_full_name": "Johan Magnus Aanderaa",
        "timestamp": 1787248295
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Hey, could you share a <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mwe.html\">#mwe</a> please? It's easier to help with a code example</p>",
        "id": 617758566,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1787248619
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also, have you tried <code>rw!</code> instead of <code>rw</code>?</p>",
        "id": 617758613,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1787248627
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>rw!</code> did it — thanks, that's exactly what I was missing. I didn't know it existed.</p>\n<p>For anyone finding this later: the situation was a sum over a dependent function type indexed by a <code>Finset</code> subtype, where rewriting the index set failed with \"motive is not type correct\" because the subset proof inside the restriction mentions the set. <code>rw!</code> handles the dependent motive where <code>rw</code> gives up.</p>\n<p>This unblocks a factorisation argument for conditional independence in a do-calculus formalisation, so it was a real one. Second time you've saved me a session, Snir — much appreciated.</p>",
        "id": 617761314,
        "sender_full_name": "Johan Magnus Aanderaa",
        "timestamp": 1787249298
    }
]